<section class="grid2" aria-label="Core overview and links">
  <div class="card">
    <h2 class="section-title">What The Core is</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Most People Ops breakdowns that look like “dashboard problems” are really contract problems:
      different definitions, different thresholds, and no clear ownership.
      The Core makes those rules explicit — so tools execute against shared truth.
    </p>

    <div class="miniGrid" aria-label="What it prevents">
      <div class="mini">
        <b>Definition drift</b>
        <span>“Time-to-fill” means different things in different places.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="mini">
        <b>Threshold drift</b>
        <span>Flags and escalations change silently over time.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="mini">
        <b>Ownership drift</b>
        <span>No one is accountable for correctness or changes.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="callout">
      <b>When The Core is present:</b> signals route cleanly → decisions stay consistent → automation stays safe → humans remain accountable.
    </div>
  </div>

